  "narrative": "Synthesis for the supplied dataset, emphasizing evidence that is directly reproducible rather than causal or generalizable claims.\n\n1. Supported central finding: feature_027 and outcome_014.  The response deadline for H14 was satisfied earlier by independent validation. H14 remains accepted: feature_027=1 versus feature_027=0 is associated with a very large positive shift in outcome_014. Discovery gave a signed estimate of about +0.796 (95% Welch interval approximately +0.776 to +0.816), and independent validation gave about +0.802 (independent interval approximately +0.775 to +0.829). Under the operational absolute clinical threshold used for these negative-valued dependency scores, the outcome_014 threshold is only about 0.009, so both discovery and validation are enormously above threshold. The many accepted stratum analyses (H39/H67 by feature_034, H40/H68 by feature_002, H73/H74 by feature_050, H77 by feature_008=0, H58 by feature_054 level_002, and H80/H81 by feature_061 age extremes) consistently estimate effects near +0.78 to +0.80 with lower bounds far above threshold. This supports a highly stable dataset-specific association across measured strata. It does not identify what feature_027 means biologically, prove causality, rule out latent pipeline/sample coding, or support external generalizability.\n\n2. New supported dataset-specific discovery: feature_050 and outcome_001.  H88 was accepted in discovery: feature_050=1 versus feature_050=0 showed a signed effect of about +0.784 for a negative-direction claim (95% Welch interval approximately +0.765 to +0.803), with adequate cell sizes (412 exposed, 1588 comparator). For outcome_001 the operational clinical threshold is about 0.042, so the lower interval bound is far above threshold. This is now one of the two largest dataset-specific associations found, alongside feature_027-outcome_014. Because the effect is extremely large and the predictor labels are opaque, the appropriate conclusion remains association within this supplied dataset only. Independent validation has not yet arrived or been incorporated for H88, and the registered feature_027-stratified refinements H96-H98 are still untested. If those strata show large effects and little interaction, the association is likely not merely an artifact of overlap with feature_027; if confined to one feature_027 stratum, it suggests effect modification or latent subgroup concentration.\n\n3. H13 response deadline.  H13 tested feature_027=1 versus 0 for a clinically meaningful positive difference in outcome_013. Discovery R27 was borderline: signed estimate about +0.0270, interval about +0.0037 to +0.0502. The point estimate is essentially at the operational outcome_013 threshold (about 0.0269), but the interval includes clinically nonmeaningful positive effects and is far from a robust accept. Independent validation R39 reversed direction: signed estimate about -0.0103, interval about -0.0513 to +0.0306. Although the validation interval barely crosses the threshold, the point estimate is negative and inconsistent with discovery. Combining discovery and validation therefore fails to support a clinically meaningful positive association and provides stronger evidence against a stable positive feature_027 effect on outcome_013. I therefore reject H13 and close it.\n\n4. Negative and selective findings.  The evidence argues against broad clinically meaningful feature_027 effects across most other CRISPR dependency outcomes. Besides H13 rejection, feature_027 positive claims were rejected for outcome_011, outcome_008, outcome_012, outcome_016, and outcome_003. H8 (outcome_006) remains unresolved but is not compelling because the independent validation estimate fell below the clinical threshold and its interval remained wide. Thus the clinically meaningful feature_027 signal appears concentrated on outcome_014 in this supplied dataset.\n\nFeature_050 is not broadly clinically meaningful either. The completed feature_050 outcome screen produced one huge selective association with outcome_001 and otherwise mostly subthreshold or inconsistent results. Several feature_050 negative claims are rejected: outcome_003, outcome_004, outcome_009, outcome_005, and outcome_016. Others are unresolved but not compelling for validation: outcome_010, outcome_012, outcome_015, and outcome_002. The pattern therefore supports selectivity rather than a global feature_050 effect across dependency scores.\n\n5. Unresolved uncertainty.  The most important unresolved questions are: (a) whether feature_050-outcome_001 is robust within feature_027 strata and whether feature_027 modifies it; (b) whether feature_054 level_002 versus level_001 has a genuine near-threshold association with outcome_014 independent of feature_027 composition, given H94/H95 point estimates above threshold but intervals crossing zero and threshold; (c) whether the remaining feature_050 screens on outcome_013, outcome_008, and outcome_011 (H61-H63) reveal another clinically meaningful association; and (d) whether other predictors beyond feature_027, feature_050, and feature_054 show meaningful effects. Interaction and additional feature_027 stratum analyses are lower priority because the central feature_027-outcome_014 association already has strong internal and independent replication.\n\n6. Most informative next analysis.  The highest-value next tests are the registered feature_027-stratified analyses for feature_050-outcome_001: H96 and H97 as mean differences within feature_027=0 and feature_027=1, and H98 as the interaction by feature_027=1. These will determine whether H88 is a broad dataset-specific association or concentrated in a latent subgroup defined by feature_027. In parallel, H61-H63 should complete the feature_050 outcome screen for outcome_013, outcome_008, and outcome_011, clarifying whether feature_050 has any additional clinically meaningful associations. I also registered an interaction claim for feature_054 on outcome_014 by feature_027=1 to directly test whether the near-threshold H94/H95 contrasts reflect effect modification rather than composition. If the feature_050-outcome_001 strata remain large and the interaction is small, the next appraise should prioritize independent validation of H88. If one stratum carries the effect or validation weakens it, the claim should be narrowed or reassessed. All conclusions remain dataset-specific associations, not causal, mechanistic, or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current evidence status after iteration 5 synthesis.\n\nAccepted and strongly supported: H14 (feature_027=1 vs 0 -> large positive outcome_014; discovery R14 +0.796, independent validation R26 +0.802, threshold ~0.009). Multiple accepted stratum claims (H39,H67,H40,H68,H73,H74,H77,H58,H80,H81) replicate the effect near +0.78 to +0.80 with lower bounds far above threshold. Interpretation limited to dataset-specific association; opaque predictors and enormous effect leave latent coding/sample-structure explanations plausible.\n\nAccepted but not independently validated yet: H88 (feature_050=1 vs 0 -> large negative-direction effect on outcome_001; signed +0.784, CI ~0.765-0.803, threshold ~0.042). H88 is scientifically meaningful within supplied discovery data. Need H96/H97/H98 (feature_027 strata and interaction) before broad validation/narrowing. If robust, request independent validation for H88 in appraise; if subgroup-specific, refine or reassess.\n\nH13 response deadline resolved: reject and close. Discovery R27 borderline positive for outcome_013 (+0.027, threshold ~0.027), but independent validation R39 reversed negative (-0.010), interval upper only slightly above threshold. Combined evidence does not support clinically meaningful positive feature_027-outcome_013 association.\n\nFeature_027 cross-outcome: mostly null/nonclinical. Rejected: H13, H15, H16, H42, H46, H52. H8 unresolved but not compelling after validation (estimate below threshold, wide interval). Central feature_027 effect appears concentrated on outcome_014.\n\nFeature_050 cross-outcome: selective. Rejected clinically meaningful negative claims: H17, H18, H19, H90, H93. Unresolved borderline: H20, H89, H91, H92. H88 is large outlier. Remaining feature_050 screens H61 (outcome_013), H62 (outcome_008), H63 (outcome_011) are active/untested and should be run next to determine whether feature_050 has any additional clinically meaningful associations.\n\nFeature_054 outcome_014: H94 within feature_027=0 estimate +0.0145 (CI -0.0044 to +0.0333); H95 within feature_027=1 estimate +0.0265 (CI -0.0145 to +0.0674), threshold ~0.0093. Point estimates above threshold but intervals not decisive. Registered interaction by feature_027=1 for outcome_014/feature_054 as a refinement of H95 to test effect modification directly.\n\nNext analyze priorities (12 cap): 1) H96-H98 feature_050-outcome_001 feature_027 strata/interaction. 2) H61-H63 remaining feature_050 outcome screens. 3) new feature_054 interaction by feature_027=1. If budget remains, H64-H66 outcome_014 other predictors (feature_045, feature_042, feature_065) are lower priority. Avoid more feature_027-outcome_014 robustness work unless heterogeneity emerges.\n\nValidation policy: H88 is highest-value validation target if strata support robustness. At most one voluntary validation per appraise; use it for H88 if H96/H97 large and H98 interaction not strongly contradicting. H94/H95 feature_054 can be considered for validation only after interaction/replication or if one stratum becomes convincing."
}
